#: Game.Levels.PerfectSecrecy.L01_XorSelfInverse
msgid "## Bits Are Just Modular Arithmetic Again\n"
"\n"
"A bit is an element of §0 — arithmetic modulo 2, the smallest ring\n"
"you've worked with yet. Addition in §1 is exactly the **XOR**\n"
"operation on bits: §2, §3, §4, and §5 (the '1' carries\n"
"away, since we're working mod 2).\n"
"\n"
"That last case is the important one: adding a bit to *itself* always gives\n"
"§6. Every element of §7 is its own additive inverse.\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Prove that every bit §8 satisfies §9.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"§10 has only two elements — Lean can just check both."
msgstr ""

