#: Game.Levels.MinRank.L04_Minor
msgid "## Minors\n"
"\n"
"A **minor** of a matrix is the determinant of a square submatrix. If A is\n"
"m x n, a k x k minor is det(A_{S,T}) where S is a subset of [m],\n"
"T is a subset of [n], |S| = |T| = k. Crucially, a minor is usually *smaller*\n"
"than the original matrix — that's the whole point of the name.\n"
"\n"
"In Mathlib, §0 extracts a submatrix using selector functions\n"
"§1, §2; §3 is the corresponding minor.\n"
"\n"
"### Cryptographic Context\n"
"\n"
"In the **Support-Minor** model (a generalization of MinRank), the attacker\n"
"exploits the fact that if rank(M) <= r, then all (r+1) x (r+1) minors of M are zero.\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"The identity matrix on §4 has a genuine 2x2 minor: the top-left block,\n"
"selected by keeping rows/columns §5 and §6 and discarding row/column §7.\n"
"Prove that this 2x2 minor equals §8.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"Every field involved here (§9) and every index (§10, §11) is\n"
"finite and concrete, so §12 can just compute both the submatrix and its\n"
"determinant directly."
msgstr ""

