#: Game.Levels.PerfectSecrecy.L02_OneTimePad
msgid "## One Function, Two Jobs\n"
"\n"
"The **one-time pad (OTP)** encrypts an §0-bit message §1 with an §2-bit\n"
"key §3 (as long as the message, used only once — hence the name) by XOR-ing\n"
"them position by position:\n"
"\n"
"    otpEncrypt k m i = m i + k i\n"
"\n"
"Unlike Caesar (which needed a separate §4 to decrypt), OTP has a striking\n"
"property: encrypting *twice* with the same key gets you back to where you\n"
"started. Decryption isn't a different operation — it's the same one.\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Prove that encrypting an OTP-encrypted message a second time, with the same\n"
"key, recovers the original message.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"Reduce to a single position with §5, unfold the definition, then\n"
"package Level 1's fact as a named intermediate step with §6 before\n"
"using it to finish."
msgstr ""

