#: Game.Levels.ClassicalCiphers.L04_ShiftComposition
msgid "## A Shift Is a Thing, Not Just a Step\n"
"\n"
"So far a 'shift' has only appeared as something you *do*: an action performed\n"
"on a letter. But a shift §0 is also a mathematical **object** in\n"
"its own right — an element of a commutative group that can itself be added,\n"
"combined, and reasoned about independently of any particular letter it acts\n"
"on.\n"
"\n"
"A **Vigenère cipher** applies a whole sequence of Caesar shifts (one per\n"
"letter of a repeating keyword). If you ever apply two independent shifts to\n"
"the same position, one after another, does the order matter?\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Prove that applying shift §1 then §2 gives the same result as applying\n"
"§3 then §4.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"Again pure ring arithmetic — commutativity and associativity of addition in\n"
"§5."
msgstr ""

