#: Game.Levels.ClassicalCiphers.L03_RoundTrip
msgid "## From Examples to a Law\n"
"\n"
"Checking §0 and §1 one number at a time would take\n"
"forever if we wanted to be sure the Caesar cipher *never* loses information.\n"
"Instead, we generalize: decrypting an encryption returns the original message\n"
"for **every** plaintext §2 and **every** shift §3 at once.\n"
"\n"
"    (m + k) - k = m\n"
"\n"
"This is no longer a single computation to check — it is an algebraic pattern\n"
"to *prove*, once and for all.\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Prove the general roundtrip law for arbitrary §4.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"§5 is a commutative ring, and this identity is pure ring arithmetic\n"
"(add then subtract the same thing). The §6 tactic (from the Tutorial\n"
"World) closes it directly — no case-by-case checking needed."
