#: Game.Levels.ClassicalCiphers.L06_Vigenere
msgid "## A Different Shift for Every Position\n"
"\n"
"The **Vigenère cipher** fixes the biggest weakness of a single Caesar shift:\n"
"instead of one key §0, it uses a whole *keyword*, repeated to match the\n"
"length of the message, and applies a different Caesar shift at each\n"
"position.\n"
"\n"
"If the message is §1 letters long, model the (already-repeated) key as a\n"
"function §2 giving one shift per position, and encrypt\n"
"position-by-position exactly like Caesar:\n"
"\n"
"    vigenereEncrypt key m i = m i + key i\n"
"    vigenereDecrypt key c i = c i - key i\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Prove that decrypting an encrypted message recovers it, at *every* position\n"
"§3 simultaneously — i.e. the two functions §4\n"
"and §5 are equal.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"Two functions on §6 are equal exactly when they agree at every input\n"
"(§7). After that, each position is the same one-position roundtrip\n"
"identity you already proved for Caesar back in Level 3."
