#: Game.Levels.ModularArithmetic.L05_Fermat
msgid "## A Theorem That Powers RSA\n"
"\n"
"You've been raising elements of §0 to powers since Level 2. Here is\n"
"the single deepest fact about that operation, when the modulus is *prime*:\n"
"for any nonzero §1 in §2, raising §3 to the power §4 always\n"
"gives back §5 — no matter which nonzero §6 you started with.\n"
"\n"
"This is **Fermat's Little Theorem**. It is not obvious from the ring axioms\n"
"alone; it's a genuine number-theoretic fact about how multiplication mixes\n"
"the nonzero elements of §7 around.\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Prove Fermat's Little Theorem: for a prime §8 and nonzero §9,\n"
"§10.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"Mathlib already has this exact theorem."
