#: Game.Levels.ClassicalCiphers.L01_CaesarEncrypt
msgid "## Letters as Numbers\n"
"\n"
"To do cryptography with Lean, we first need to turn letters into numbers. Map\n"
"§0 to §1, and work modulo 26 so that shifting past §2\n"
"wraps back around to §3. In Lean, the type of integers modulo §4 is\n"
"**§5**.\n"
"\n"
"### The Caesar Cipher\n"
"\n"
"The **Caesar cipher** encrypts a letter §6 (plaintext) with a secret shift\n"
"§7 by computing:\n"
"\n"
"    c = m + k   (mod 26)\n"
"\n"
"For example, with shift §8, the letter §9 (which is §10) encrypts to\n"
"§11 (which is §12), since §13.\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Check this concrete example: encrypting §14 with shift §15 gives §16.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"§17 is a finite type with decidable equality, so Lean can simply\n"
"*compute* both sides and compare them. The §18 tactic does exactly this."
msgstr ""

