#: Game.Levels.ModularArithmetic.L06_Euler
msgid "## Beyond Prime Moduli\n"
"\n"
"Fermat's Little Theorem needed a *prime* modulus. Real cryptosystems like\n"
"RSA use a modulus §0 — a product of two primes, not prime itself.\n"
"**Euler's Theorem** is exactly Fermat's theorem generalized to work for\n"
"*any* modulus §1, replacing 'nonzero' with the right general condition\n"
"('coprime to §2') and replacing the exponent §3 with **Euler's\n"
"totient** §4 (written §5): the count of numbers below §6 that\n"
"share no common factor with it.\n"
"\n"
"    Fermat:  a coprime to p (prime)   ⟹  a ^ (p - 1)      ≡ 1 (mod p)\n"
"    Euler:   a coprime to n (any n)   ⟹  a ^ (totient n)  ≡ 1 (mod n)\n"
"\n"
"When §7 is prime, §8 and Euler's theorem *is* Fermat's.\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Prove Euler's Theorem: if §9 and §10 are coprime, then\n"
"§11.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"Mathlib already has this exact theorem too — it even calls it by name."
msgstr ""

