#: Game.Levels.UOV.L01_QuadraticFromMatrix
msgid "## What 'Quadratic' Actually Means\n"
"\n"
"UOV's central map §0 is described as 'quadratic' — but so far in this\n"
"course, every map you've formalized (Modular Arithmetic's homomorphisms,\n"
"Matrix Algebra's transposes) has been *linear*. Quadratic is different, and\n"
"Mathlib makes the difference precise: a quadratic map §1 comes from a\n"
"**bilinear** map §2 (a matrix, in coordinates) by\n"
"plugging the *same* input into both of its slots: §3.\n"
"\n"
"This is also exactly why a quadratic map can't be a §4: doubling\n"
"§5 doesn't double §6, it quadruples it (§7),\n"
"which breaks linearity outright.\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Prove that §8, evaluated at §9, really does equal\n"
"§10.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"Mathlib already has this exact fact — it's essentially the definition."
msgstr ""
